node_modules/
site/node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.vercel/

# adna-mcp-server build output (P3.3). Not committed: `prepublishOnly` rebuilds
# it, so the published tarball can never carry a stale dist/ — and a tarball is
# never assembled from whatever happened to be on disk.
mcp/dist/
mcp/*.tgz

# Playwright test artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# compliance_checker.py output — a read-only audit tool must not dirty the tree (F-MER-A3, v8.9).
# Default outdir is ./.compliance_out; the two report names are ignored belt-and-suspenders in case --outdir . is used.
.compliance_out/
compliance_report.md
compliance_scorecard.yaml

# Hero image-gen candidates (heavy intermediates; finals committed, provenance in image_gen_log JSONs)
site/src/assets/heroes/candidates/

# Evidence artifacts — heavy capture binaries + raw Lighthouse dumps (Refit M4 / DP5, 2026-07-23).
# Reproducible via scripts/visual_capture.mjs / Lighthouse; capture_report.json provenance +
# synthesis notes stay committed. Policy: how/campaigns/campaign_refit/artifacts/evidence_artifact_policy.md
how/campaigns/campaign_storyweave/artifacts/onboarding_references/**/*.png
how/missions/artifacts/storyweave_p3_measure/**/*.png
how/missions/artifacts/storyweave_p4_docs_ia/**/*.png
how/missions/artifacts/storyweave_p4_docs_ia/lighthouse/
how/missions/artifacts/storyweave_p5_measure/**/*.png
how/missions/artifacts/storyweave_p5_m5_3/**/*.png
how/missions/artifacts/storyweave_p5_m5_3/lighthouse/
# HAUSSMANN capture estate (wind-down 2026-08-20) — the same Refit policy, applied to this campaign.
# Applied in the policy's DANGLE-SAFE ORDER: the 61 PNGs individually cited by committed docs were
# `git add`ed FIRST (git keeps tracked files tracked regardless of these patterns), so what follows
# ignores only the 126 uncited sweep frames. Reversing that order is the policy's named inverse trap —
# "gitignoring evidence a committed claim still cites recreates the dangle."
# Regenerate any ignored frame with: node scripts/visual_capture.mjs --base <url> --routes … --axe
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/evidence/captures_p1_2/**/*.png
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/evidence/captures_p1_4/**/*.png
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/evidence/captures_p2_2/**/*.png
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/evidence/p1_1_captures/**/*.png
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/evidence/dossier/captures/**/*.png
# P4.1 (2026-08-23) — same policy, but the cited frames are held by EXPLICIT NEGATION rather than by
# having been `git add`ed first. The tracked-first order works only while the files stay tracked: a
# `git reset` during staging re-exposed them to the pattern and the add failed. Negation states the
# exception in the file itself, so it survives a reset, a fresh clone, and an agent who does not know
# the ordering rule. (The blocks above are left as-is — their files are long since committed.)
# ⚠ The outage set is NOT regenerable — the pre-2026-08-18 build it captures is gone. What survives of
# it is deliberately the part that carries the evidence: the two cited frames plus the report
# (per-surface status, title, h1, bodyLen), which is what the F-s finding actually argues from.
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures/**/*.png

# P4.1 O2/O3 (2026-08-24) — the `captures_o2` estate, same Refit policy, same DANGLE-SAFE order:
# the frames a committed doc argues FROM are held by EXPLICIT NEGATION below; the 21 uncited sweep
# frames (17.5 MB) are ignored and are REGENERABLE — unlike the outage set, the build they capture is
# `site/dist` from `site/src` at commit 9608820, which is committed.
#   node scripts/visual_capture.mjs --base http://localhost:4321 \
#     --routes /vaults/,/design-system/,/get-started/ --viewports mobile-lg,tablet,desktop \
#     --themes dark,light --axe --out <out>
# The three provenance JSONs (capture_report / axe_dark / axe_light) are NOT ignored and stay committed
# — per-surface status, title, h1, bodyLen and the axe result are what the claims actually argue from.
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/**/*.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/vaults__desktop__light.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/vaults__desktop__dark.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/get-started__desktop__light.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/zero_result__desktop__light.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/zero_result__desktop__dark.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_o2/design-system__desktop__dark.png
# ⚠ `zero_result__desktop__dark` was added to this list only after a `--no-index` check: it had been
# COMMITTED at O2 while the new pattern said ignore it. `git check-ignore` does NOT report tracked
# files by default, so the first verification pass came back clean *because the files were staged* —
# a check that cannot see the state it exists to find. Verify ignore rules with `--no-index`.
how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures_outage_20260823/**/*.png
# — cited frames, deliberately kept (4 craft/slot evidence + 2 outage evidence):
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures/home__desktop__dark.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures/home__desktop__light.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures/learn__desktop__dark.png
!how/campaigns/campaign_haussmann/artifacts/p4_1/captures/vaults__desktop__dark.png
